## Summary

I built a production-polished native Apple/SwiftUI parity of the web `TirePressureSection` as 8 files under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/TirePressureSection.*`, following the established surface convention (`AcDcStatsPanel`/`SpeedTrendChart`).

**What shipped**
- **Adapter** (pure, Foundation-only): wheel enum, sample/row/tile models, projection (per-wheel min/max over positive readings, plotted-wheel + flattened-row derivations, `hasAnyReading`, axis bounds), `fmtNumber` port, surface slug, VoiceOver builder.
- **Model**: P1/S8 `TirePressureSectionSource` state-holder seam + `@Observable` model, P1/S10 i18n facade, P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry, input→resolved projection, in-memory source.
- **Views + Chart**: per-wheel min/max tiles, a four-series **Swift Charts** `LineMark` chart (monotone/no-dots/width-2/connect-nulls per `AREA_DEFAULTS`) with FL/FR/RL/RR mapped to **exact brand-token colors**, selection tooltip, legend, and loading/empty/error chrome.
- **Main view**: composes header + freshness chip + connectivity banner + state switch (loading/empty/error/data/stale/offline).
- **Previews** (×6 states), **Tests** (adapter + resolver-per-state + model wiring/telemetry/freshness + a11y), **strings** (all web-parity keys + envelope).

**Key correctness fix:** the module already had `TirePressure*` dashboard-widget types — I namespaced every surface type as `TirePressureSection*` to avoid duplicate-definition collisions.

